# Environment for the real-SDK E2B integration suite.
#
# Copy this file to .env.test in this same directory and fill in your
# own values:
#
#   cp backend/tests/integration/.env.test.example \
#      backend/tests/integration/.env.test
#
# .env.test is gitignored (it holds a real API key) and is loaded by
# tests/integration/conftest.py, so it resolves the same way whether you
# run run-integration-tests.sh or a bare `pytest tests/integration/...`.
# Variables already present in your shell environment take precedence
# over this file, so CI can inject secrets without a file on disk. Point
# at a different file with MCPOLIS_INTEGRATION_ENV=/path/to/file.
#
# These tests hit the live E2B API and spend real money (sandbox-
# seconds). They auto-skip when no E2B key is set.

# --- Required: E2B API key --------------------------------------------
# Your E2B API key. Get one at https://e2b.dev/dashboard.
MCPOLIS_E2B_API_KEY=

# --- Optional: test knob ----------------------------------------------
# Reattach-stall stress test (test_e2b_reattach_stall_recovery_e2e.py):
# number of pause/reattach cycles to run. Defaults to 6 when unset;
# raise it to harden the reattach path.
# STRESS_CYCLES=6

# --- Optional: orphan-sandbox cleanup tooling -------------------------
# Used only by the run-on-demand list_orphan_sandboxes.py script, not by
# the pytest suite. Scope orphan detection to one instance id; when
# unset, every tagged sandbox is considered.
# MCPOLIS_INSTANCE_ID=
# Comma/space-separated sandbox ids to treat as still-persisted (not
# orphans) during cleanup, usually produced from a Mongo query.
# MCPOLIS_PERSISTED_SANDBOX_IDS=
